# A backtick-escaped LOCAL is still mangled at emission (#1357), so it collides with its
# case-differing twin exactly as a bare name would — `zed` and `Zed` both emit `zed`, and the
# generated C# would be CS0128. The refusal says so rather than pointing at a remedy that does not
# work for locals; for TYPES the escape does preserve the spelling.

def main() -> None:
    zed: int = 6
    `Zed`: int = 7
    print(zed)
    print(`Zed`)
